s  and just kind of take across the middle  and this is just an optional step this  is just for presentation purposes  i just like the way it looks when it  comes out of the oven like this  and then i'm going to take the other  half of so that's a half of a lemon then  i'm going to go ahead and squeeze the  other half  just on top just like that  okay these are ready for the oven and so  when you roast when you roast asparagus  it just gets this texture and then  the tops of them get all roasted and  toasty brown and everything about it is  just delicious  don't ever boil your or steam your  asparagus that's the most boring way  if you like it that way fine but i'm  just telling you it kicks it up 10  notches when you do it this way  let's get this in the oven and i have  one that's in there already  if it's done it probably goes for about  15 minutes i would say  and then it comes out just looking  spectacular  and i would say that i would just serve  it just like this i don't even want to  try to take it off and put it on a  platter  or anything like that just because i  love the way that it looks  and it's just so springy and perfect for  really any time of year as long as your  asparagus are in season  go ahead and get it you can find all of  these things at your  local smiths of course in the produce  section you're always going to find  asparagus and lemons  thank you so much for watching thank you  for shopping and we'll see you all next  time bye-bye  if you want that recipe and ingredients  you can visit smithsfoodanddrug.com  and we
 

